<!--
NIGHT-RUN BRIEF — copy to ~/.claude/night/brief.md before arming a night mode.

*** THIS FILE IS THE MEMORY ACROSS CRASHES. ***

When the watchdog relaunches Claude after a crash, an error, or a usage-limit
lockout, the restarted session has NO memory of the conversation that armed the
run. It re-reads this file and nothing else. If it is thin, the restart resumes
blind.

WRITE IT SO IT IS SELF-SUFFICIENT. Assume the reader knows nothing: not the
project, not the goal, not what was already tried. Name the working directory,
name the documents, spell out the tasks. Redundancy costs nothing here and
ambiguity costs the night.

The agent APPENDS to this file as it works. Do not treat it as static — DONE,
BLOCKED, and OPEN grow through the run, and that growth is what a restarted
session reads to know where it got to.

PRE-FLIGHT: confirm ~/.claude/night/ holds more than just the watchdog script
before arming. A run with no brief is a run that cannot survive its first
restart.

Delete this comment block when you fill the file in.
-->

