## GOAL

<!--
One falsifiable, bounded sentence — the same sentence given to /goal.

This is the standard the agent measures candidate work against when it has to
decide what to do next. It matters most under /nightmax, where running out of
assigned work is not a finish condition: without a goal, "most valuable task"
is undefined and the agent optimises for whatever is nearest.

  Good: "Get the engine through Stage 3 with the fidelity suite green, and do
        not begin any client work."
  Bad:  "Make progress on the app."
-->

---

## TASKS

<!--
An explicit numbered checklist of every task tonight. Specific and concrete —
a restarted session may have nothing but this file to go on.

Each item should name what "done" looks like. "Fix the importer" is not a task;
"fix the importer so `npm run test:import` exits zero" is.

Under /nightmax, add a `## Self-directed queue` section below this one for work
the agent picks itself. It appends chosen work there BEFORE starting it, so the
record shows what it chose and why.
-->

