## DONE

<!--
Appended by the agent as each item completes. One line each: what was done,
which task it closes, and the commit SHA.

This is the first thing a restarted session reads. Without it, a restart
re-does finished work — or worse, half-re-does it.
-->

---

## BLOCKED

<!--
Anything that cannot proceed, with WHY. A blocker is not "this was hard" — it
is a dependency that is genuinely unavailable: a missing credential, a service
that will not start, a decision only a human can make.

Under /nightmin, everything being done or blocked is the finish condition, so
this section is load-bearing: a task parked here ends the night, and a task
parked here wrongly ends it early.
-->

---

## OPEN

<!--
*** THE LOG-AND-PROCEED BUCKET. ***

The agent cannot ask a question during a night run. So when it finds something
genuinely ambiguous that neither the PRD nor the pipeline doc covers, the
protocol is: RECORD IT HERE, PROCEED WITH THE MOST CONSERVATIVE OPTION, KEEP
GOING.

Each entry needs three things:
  - what was ambiguous
  - what was chosen instead
  - what would change if the choice was wrong

This section is the highest-value thing you read in the morning. Every entry is
a place the two documents failed, and it is the direct input to the next
revision of the PRD — most entries should end up as a row in PRD §18 or §20.
-->
